  "body": "Implement the core 4-axis cylindrical flow-line toolpath kernel in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_flow.rs`.\n\nWhat to build:\n- Accept picked 3D guide edge chains, part facets, a rotary `Axis` (provided by the #2772 stated-axis resolver), `RotaryFlowParams`, and `AxisControl`.\n- Require a ball-nose tool and at least two guide chains in this first slice; refuse empty, off-model, or single-chain inputs by name.\n- Unwrap each chain into continuous cylindrical `(theta, v)` coordinates about `Axis` using `unwrap_near`, and align chain pairs by nearest `2 * pi` offset.\n- Parameterize the pair by normalized arc length, compute developed width `(s = R_ref * theta, v)`, and choose pass count from `stepover` or `scallop_stepover(r, tolerance)`.\n- Adaptively chord each interpolated flow curve within `ARC_FIT_TOL` / `tolerance`.\n- Compute gouge-free radial ball centers `rho_ball(theta, v)` where `min_tri dist(center, tri) >= r` via `closest_pt_tri`, so steep helical flanks never gouge.\n- Link passes radially on the retract cylinder (matching `rotary_links`) and emit tool tips via `retip` and `command_axis`.\n\nProvenance: published 4-axis cylindrical unwrapping and iso-parametric flow-line CAM literature; no vendor material consulted.\n\nDepends on #2772 for stated rotary axis resolution on helical models.\n\nDone means: `crates/motion::multiaxis::rotary_flow` generates gouge-free, radially posed passes across multi-turn helical bands on a rotor mesh in `crates/motion/tests/` and refuses invalid or single-chain inputs by name.\n\nPart of #2804\n",
